<appwidget-provider
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:minWidth="180dp"
    android:minHeight="72dp"
    android:targetCellWidth="3"
    android:targetCellHeight="1"
    android:initialLayout="@layout/widget_pen_mode"
    android:previewLayout="@layout/widget_pen_mode"
    android:resizeMode="horizontal"
    android:widgetCategory="home_screen"
    android:description="@string/pen_mode_widget_description"
    android:updatePeriodMillis="0" />
<!--
     minHeight was 40dp against a layout that needs ~72dp: 14+14 dp padding plus a
     44 dp icon disc. The declared values do reach the framework verbatim
     (`dumpsys appwidget` printed min=(28161x10241), i.e. 110<<8|1 and 40<<8|1), so
     the old numbers were a real under-declaration and a host was free to render
     the widget clipped.

     description was @string/touch_mode_footer — the 700-character settings-page
     footer, shown verbatim under the widget's name in the picker. Now a sentence.

     targetCellWidth 3 rather than 2: at TARGET_SCREEN_DENSITY 320 on a 6-column
     grid, two cells is not enough for "350 Hz touch · no stylus" beside a 44 dp
     disc, and a widget whose own subtitle is ellipsised in its default size is
     not finished.

     updatePeriodMillis 0 is right and deliberate: nothing here polls. Updates are
     pushed by PenModeController whenever the mode changes.
-->
